  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Spanish distinguishes between two past tenses: past I (preterite) for definite, completed actions, and past II (imperfect) for ongoing or habitual actions. Choosing between them conveys whether an event is seen as a single whole or as background to another action."
    }
